Q4 (Hard). Which viewer pays the least per hour of watching? Only look at viewers with at least 5 watch entries. For each viewer:

monthsActive = (2026 − joinYear) × 12 + (6 − joinMonth) + 1
total paid = monthlyFee × monthsActive
hours watched = sum of minutesWatched ÷ 60
cost per hour = total paid ÷ hours watched

Return the viewer with the lowest cost per hour.

{
  "viewerId": "V-4098",
  "name": "Max Brown",
  "plan": "basic",
  "monthsActive": 2,
  "hoursWatched": 11.12,
  "costPerHour": 26.81
}

Q4 is hard because it combines three things. You work out the months from the join date, multiply by the plan fee, and add up minutes inside the nested watchHistory, then divide the two. I checked that none of the four answers has a tie.